      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Reactive oxygen species (ROS) are thought to contribute to the progression of cardiovascular disease (CVD). At present, it has been known that the NADH/NADPH oxidase system is the major source of superoxide in the vascular system. Cytochrome b-245 (P22phox), which is a critical component of NADH/NADPH oxidase, plays an important role in electron transport and producing the superoxide anion. It is considerable to take attention to whether the polymorphism of P22phox gene is associated with a risk of coronary heart disease (CHD). To distinguish the relationship between them will be beneficial to elucidate the genetic mechanisms of CHD, and develop a new genetic marker to provide theoretical base for the prevention and cure of CHD."},
